11. Reaffirms its commitment to a just, lasting and comprehensive peace in the Middle East based on the two-State solution, with Israel and Palestine living side by side in peace within secure and recognized borders based on the 1967 lines, in accordance with relevant United Nations resolutions and mutually agreed parameters, and recalls resolution 2334 (2016);

12. Calls for renewed and coordinated diplomatic efforts by the international community, including the Quartet and regional partners, to de-escalate the situation, protect civilians, secure the release of hostages, provide humanitarian assistance, and create conditions for a return to meaningful negotiations on all final status issues;

13. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

